but the tykes love it.

09:44.522 --> 09:46.752
Oh, boy, I wish my doctor
had a sense of humor.

09:46.924 --> 09:49.484
Every time I have a prostate exam,
I say:

09:49.660 --> 09:52.595
"What? You're not gonna
buy me dinner first?"

09:52.763 --> 09:56.199
- And nothing. Not even a smile.
- Really? Because that's a beaut.

09:56.367 --> 09:59.632
That's what I thought,
but most people just don't get me.

10:00.238 --> 10:02.934
Well, that's their loss.

10:08.713 --> 10:11.648
Excuse me. Uh-oh.

10:12.917 --> 10:14.407
Hi, Judith.

10:14.585 --> 10:16.382
I just stopped for a bite to eat.

10:17.755 --> 10:19.518
I know you have leftover meatloaf.

10:19.690 --> 10:21.783
Probably leftover
from when I was married to her.

10:21.959 --> 10:23.221
Shh!

10:24.895 --> 10:26.362
What?

10:26.530 --> 10:28.191
That was Alan.

10:28.366 --> 10:30.357
- Yes, that Alan.
- Hi, Judith.

10:31.035 --> 10:34.027
No, no, Jake's not here,
just the two of us.

10:34.205 --> 10:36.173
No, I have not lost my mind.

10:36.774 --> 10:40.801
Whoa. Whoa.
Calm down. Judith, calm down.

10:40.978 --> 10:43.105
Can we talk about this
when I get home?

10:43.281 --> 10:45.715
All right, bye.

10:46.917 --> 10:48.885
She says "hi" back.

10:49.320 --> 10:52.084
- Sorry to get you in trouble.
- No trouble. I'm a grown man.

10:52.256 --> 10:54.224
I can have lunch with whoever I want.

10:54.692 --> 10:57.923
- Right.
- So how's the chiropractor biz?

10:58.095 --> 11:00.563
Well, it's been a little slow,
with the economy.

11:00.731 --> 11:02.892
But I'm starting to see
a little turnaround...

11:03.067 --> 11:04.898
I'm sorry, I gotta go.

11:13.644 --> 11:15.509
&lt;i>Oh, Celeste&lt;/i>

11:15.713 --> 11:17.772
&lt;i>You are the best&lt;/i>

11:18.249 --> 11:20.911
&lt;i>With you I was blessed&lt;/i>

11:21.085 --> 11:23.986
&lt;i>But I failed the test&lt;/i>

11:24.155 --> 11:26.350
&lt;i>And now I'm depressed&lt;/i>

11:27.425 --> 11:29.256
&lt;i>Celeste&lt;/i>

11:30.294 --> 11:32.524
&lt;i>You might as well&lt;/i>

11:33.497 --> 11:35.727
&lt;i>Take my heart&lt;/i>

11:36.634 --> 11:38.795
&lt;i>Out of my chest&lt;/i>

11:39.470 --> 11:41.631
&lt;i>And mail it&lt;/i>

11:42.006 --> 11:44.873
&lt;i>All the way to Budapest&lt;/i>

11:48.346 --> 11:50.109
- Got a minute?
- I'm busy.

11:50.281 --> 11:54.377
Yeah, I heard. Budapest. Very catchy.

11:54.819 --> 11:56.047
What do you want?

11:56.821 --> 12:00.382
I want to apologize for sending you
down a bad road with your girlfriend.

12:00.558 --> 12:04.221
- Well, forget it. I'm gonna get her back.
- Good. Good. So, what's the plan?

12:04.395 --> 12:06.829
I'm gonna finish my song
and then sing it to her.

12:07.298 --> 12:10.131
Okay. Is that the entire plan?

12:10.301 --> 12:11.461
No.

12:11.635 --> 12:13.660
I'm also gonna put on a clean shirt.

12:13.838 --> 12:16.329
Ohh. Pulling out the big guns.

12:17.575 --> 12:18.633
Yup.

12:19.043 --> 12:20.772
Can I offer an alternative plan?

12:20.945 --> 12:23.641
- I don't want any more plans from you.
- Understandable.

12:23.814 --> 12:26.977
I'd be a little skeptical in your shoes,
but just hear me out.

12:27.418 --> 12:30.785
The song, good as it is,
it smacks of desperation.

12:31.989 --> 12:33.513
Thank you.

12:35.092 --> 12:39.290
No. No. I mean, girls don't generally
respond to desperation.

12:39.730 --> 12:41.595
- How do you know?
- Are you kidding?

12:41.799 --> 12:44.927
I've been watching your father
get shot down for 25 years.

12:45.102 --> 12:48.196
It's like living
with an Air Force training film.

12:49.673 --> 12:52.870
Listen, if you really wanna
get Celeste back...

12:53.043 --> 12:56.877
...you man up, go to her house, admit
you made a mistake with the other girl...

12:57.047 --> 13:00.244
...you realize now Celeste
is one in a million, blah, blah, blah...

13:00.418 --> 13:03.410
...and if she doesn't ever
wanna see you again, you understand.

13:03.587 --> 13:05.817
And then sing her the song?

13:06.323 --> 13:07.654
Forget the song.

13:08.025 --> 13:09.720
Okay.

13:09.894 --> 13:12.192
Do I really say "blah, blah, blah"?

13:17.067 --> 13:18.500
Alan, wait.

13:18.669 --> 13:21.229
- You forgot your kabob.
- Oh, thank you.

13:21.405 --> 13:23.669
- You're welcome.
- And thanks again for driving.

13:23.874 --> 13:25.967
- It was fun.
- Yeah, I had a good time too.

13:26.143 --> 13:29.909
I'm glad.
So we should do it again sometime.

13:30.414 --> 13:32.507
- I'd like that.
- Great. Great.

13:32.683 --> 13:35.811
I'm gonna go to the flea market
tomorrow. You wanna join me?

13:36.187 --> 13:39.156
Tomorrow? Oh, gee. I don't know.

13:39.323 --> 13:43.623
- Oh, I'm sorry, it's probably too soon.
- No, no.

13:43.794 --> 13:46.729
- No, it's not, it's just...
- Judith. I know. I know.

13:46.897 --> 13:50.230
- I'm just not sure what to tell her.
- You can tell her the truth.

13:51.268 --> 13:53.099
What is the truth, Alan?

13:54.705 --> 13:57.572
- That we're friends.
- We are friends, aren't we?

13:58.776 --> 14:02.576
- Okay, friend. I'll see you tomorrow.
- It's a date.

14:12.690 --> 14:14.851
Oh! Jake. Jake. Hi, buddy.

14:15.025 --> 14:17.960
I don't care, I got my own problems.

14:24.501 --> 14:27.231
&lt;i>Oh, Celeste&lt;/i>

14:27.404 --> 14:30.168
&lt;i>I am congested&lt;/i>

14:30.374 --> 14:32.774
&lt;i>With love&lt;/i>

14:32.943 --> 14:36.640
&lt;i>For my Celested&lt;/i>

14:37.648 --> 14:38.774
&lt;i>Yeah&lt;/i>

14:41.685 --> 14:43.676
