16:04.301 --> 16:09.398
- Goodbye, Alan.
- Our marriage, that was unnatural.

16:09.573 --> 16:13.202
You can't do this, Judith.
You cannot keep us apart.

16:13.377 --> 16:15.675
Herb and I will find a way
to be together.

16:19.416 --> 16:21.145
- Hi.
- Hi.

16:21.785 --> 16:25.050
- That must've sounded kind of strange.
- Not at all.

16:25.222 --> 16:28.020
Herb is a very handsome man.

16:33.130 --> 16:37.624
- Hey, I brought you another soda.
- Thanks.

16:43.207 --> 16:46.267
Believe me, Jake,
you'll get over Celeste.

16:46.443 --> 16:48.570
I don't want to.
I think she was the one.

16:49.079 --> 16:50.307
The one what?

16:50.481 --> 16:52.642
The one who was pretty
and liked me...

16:52.816 --> 16:55.376
...and maybe was gonna let me
do stuff to her someday.

16:55.552 --> 16:58.146
And you think there's only one
of those out there?

16:58.322 --> 17:00.290
What do you think?

17:00.457 --> 17:02.516
It doesn't matter what I think.

17:03.427 --> 17:08.160
Jake, you gotta start looking
at this differently.

17:08.332 --> 17:12.530
Women are kind of like the little boxes
of cereal in one of those variety packs.

17:12.703 --> 17:14.933
- I like the variety packs.
- I know you do.

17:15.105 --> 17:18.768
They should put in more sugary cereals
and less cereals that help you poop.

17:18.942 --> 17:20.102
No argument.

17:20.277 --> 17:24.213
But my point is the variety-pack
approach gives you a choice.

17:24.381 --> 17:25.814
It's not that great a choice.

17:25.983 --> 17:28.918
In a pack of eight,
there's at least three pooping cereals.

17:29.086 --> 17:32.180
We're getting away from the point.
What's your favorite cereal?

17:32.589 --> 17:35.456
It used to be Franken Berry,
but Froot Loops now.

17:35.626 --> 17:37.594
- Terrific.
- They don't get soggy as fast.

17:37.761 --> 17:39.524
- Got it.
- Milk tastes better afterward.

17:39.696 --> 17:44.759
Okay, okay, okay.
So imagine Celeste is Froot Loops.

17:44.935 --> 17:48.530
You like her now, but who's to say
she isn't tomorrow's Franken Berry?

17:48.705 --> 17:51.799
You're wrong.
Celeste will always be my Froot Loops.

17:51.975 --> 17:54.842
You can't know that. Look at me.

17:55.012 --> 17:58.914
I've been with a lot of women, but I
only recently found the love of my life.

17:59.450 --> 18:01.611
Well, no disrespect,
but I don't wanna wait...

18:01.785 --> 18:05.744
...till I'm as old and hard up as you are
to find a good girlfriend.

18:05.923 --> 18:08.892
What? I said no disrespect.

18:09.093 --> 18:12.221
You know, you make it really difficult
to love you sometimes.

18:12.396 --> 18:15.092
Yeah, that's what my mom says.

18:20.170 --> 18:21.762
Told you I'm not an idiot.

18:30.914 --> 18:32.108
Herb.

18:32.916 --> 18:34.611
Herb.

18:42.426 --> 18:44.155
- Alan?
- Over here.

18:48.332 --> 18:51.495
- Hi.
- Didn't want you to think I stood you up.

18:51.668 --> 18:55.627
Oh. I know you'd never do that.
Judith just doesn't understand.

18:55.806 --> 18:57.433
I know, and I'm sorry.

18:57.641 --> 19:00.701
- But what are we gonna do?
- I don't know.

19:01.278 --> 19:04.839
Well, maybe I'll see you
when I bring Jake back.

19:05.649 --> 19:06.843
That'd be nice.

19:08.051 --> 19:09.518
Bye.

19:10.187 --> 19:11.654
Bye.

19:12.556 --> 19:13.682
Alan, wait.

19:14.424 --> 19:15.891
I'm coming with you.

19:16.059 --> 19:17.856
But how?

19:19.296 --> 19:23.357
- Be careful, you big galoot.
- I'm okay. I'm okay.

19:24.468 --> 19:25.901
I'm not okay!

19:27.271 --> 19:29.296
Oh, God. Herb, talk to me.

19:30.674 --> 19:32.141
What's going on out here?

19:35.646 --> 19:38.547
Alan, wait. Take me with you.

19:43.353 --> 19:46.754
- I miss Celeste.
- I miss Chelsea.

19:46.924 --> 19:48.687
I miss Herb.

19:50.761 --> 19:55.323
&lt;i>I mean, Sex and the City.
I miss Sex and the City.&lt;/i>

19:55.499 --> 19:58.195
Yeah, Alan, that's much less gay.

19:59.903 --> 20:02.929
I guess that's just what our lives
have come down to.

20:03.140 --> 20:07.133
Three pathetic, lonely guys watching
television on a Sunday night.

20:08.745 --> 20:10.303
Oh, crap, it's Sunday night.

20:10.480 --> 20:13.210
- Chelsea's flying into LAX.
- You going to pick her up?

20:13.383 --> 20:16.443
No, I'm gonna call her a cab
and take a Viagra.

20:17.855 --> 20:20.881
Well, buddy, I guess it's you and me.

20:21.058 --> 20:23.822
No disrespect, Dad,
but that just makes it worse.

20:25.796 --> 20:27.559
I said no disrespect.

20:27.731 --> 20:29.289
Why doesn't that ever work?

20:34.605 --> 20:35.936
Hello?

20:36.106 --> 20:37.698
Yeah, this is Jake.

20:37.875 --> 20:40.002
Oh, hi, Nicole.

20:40.177 --> 20:42.372
Yeah, I broke up with Celeste.

20:42.546 --> 20:45.242
Now? Sure. See you in a few.

20:46.416 --> 20:48.816
- I'm gonna meet Nicole at the pier.
- Who's Nicole?

20:48.986 --> 20:50.920
I'm not really sure.

21:24.955 --> 21:26.650
- Herb.
- We haven't got much time.

21:26.823 --> 21:29.018
Judith thinks I'm in physical therapy.

21:29.226 --> 21:31.956
Well, then let's make the most of it.
